<!-- Phase 5 website teaching layer; original chapter remains read-only. Evidence: website/reviews/android-phase5-findings.md. -->

<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">A video tile expands to full screen and starts again from the beginning. Background audio then stops when the Activity disappears. These are ownership decisions: the player, its visible surface and its controller do not need the same lifetime.</p>

<!-- @after 2. Session Layer: Background Playback and External Control :: visual -->
### Objects with different jobs

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-grid" style="--cols:2"><div class="node"><strong>Player</strong><small>Playback state and media operations.</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Surface</strong><small>Where video is displayed.</small></div><div class="node"><strong>MediaSession</strong><small>Exposes playback to permitted controllers.</small></div><div class="node"><strong>UI controller</strong><small>Connects the screen to session commands and state.</small></div></div><figcaption>For service-owned playback, the UI can disconnect while the service continues to own playback.</figcaption></figure>

