### Transfer presentation without losing the owner

<figure class="stepper"><span class="stepper-title">A chosen player moves from tile to full screen</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="node" data-el="player"><strong>Playback module</strong><small data-text="playerV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="tile"><strong>Feed tile</strong><small data-text="tileV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="full"><strong>Full-screen UI</strong><small data-text="fullV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
{
"label": "Tile visible",
"caption": "The playback module has selected the player for this item.",
"state": {
"player": "active",
"tile": "active"
},
"text": {
"playerV": "item X; position P",
"tileV": "attached video surface",
"fullV": "not visible"
},
"add": [
"player",
"tile",
"full"
]
},
{
"label": "Open full screen",
"caption": "Attach the full-screen surface first, then detach the tile, so the player never runs without a surface. Media3's PlayerView.switchTargetView uses this order for a smoother switch.",
"state": {
"tile": "ghost",
"full": "active"
},
"text": {
"tileV": "detached",
"fullV": "surface attached"
}
},
{
"label": "Same playback",
"caption": "The same chosen player retains its media state; avoid creating a second independent playback operation.",
"state": {
"player": "done"
},
"text": {
"playerV": "same item and evolving position"
}
},
{
"label": "End ownership",
"caption": "When the owning playback operation ends, release its resources deliberately.",
"state": {
"player": "ghost",
"full": "ghost"
},
"text": {
"playerV": "released when no longer needed",
"fullV": "detached"
}
}
]</script><figcaption>This illustrates one transfer policy. A product may need multiple players; measure its resource budget and verify lifecycle behaviour.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after 7. Observability :: check -->
### Try the decision

<details><summary>Cache bytes equal a durable download?</summary>

No. Offline state also needs managed download progress and, for protected content, license lifecycle.
</details>

<details><summary>Rotation should recreate service playback?</summary>

A service-owned session can retain playback while the screen reconnects its controller.
</details>

<details><summary>Only measure app crashes?</summary>

Measure first-frame time, stalls, rendition choices, DRM and download failures too.
</details>
